897	     * ignored (a {@code null} key never equals the sought key). The create endpoint's duplicate
898	     * checks reduce both an existing owner and the owner being created to the same canonical key;
899	     * this returns the matched existing owner itself, so a caller can either reject the collision or
900	     * record which owner was matched. Owners flagged deleted (soft-deleted) are excluded, so a
901	     * collision with only a deleted owner is not reported and the create is allowed.
