978	     * (e.g. no postcode) has no shared household and counts as a household of one. The value feeds the
979	     * household factor of the owner's membership points.
980	     *
981	     * @param owner the owner whose household size is being derived
982	     * @return the number of owners in the owner's household (at least {@code 1})
983	     */
984	    private int householdSize(Owner owner) {
985	        if (owner.getHouseholdId() == null) {
986	            return 1;
987	        }
988	        return householdMembers(owner).size();
989	    }
990	
991	    /**
992	     * The existing owners that make up the given owner's household: those sharing its
993	     * {@code householdId} (see {@link #householdId(Owner)}). An owner with no {@code householdId}
994	     * (e.g. no postcode) belongs to no shared household, so the result is empty. Whether the owner
995	     * itself appears depends on when the scan runs relative to the create's save: a scan taken after
996	     * the owner is persisted (as the {@link #householdSize(Owner) household size} derivation is)
997	     * counts it among its household, while one taken before the save sees only the owners already
998	     * present. Holding the household lookup in one place lets every household-derived value read the
999	     * same set of members.
1000	     *
1001	     * @param owner the owner whose household members are wanted
1002	     * @return the owners sharing the owner's household, or an empty list when it has no household
1003	     */
1004	    private List<Owner> householdMembers(Owner owner) {
1005	        String household = owner.getHouseholdId();
1006	        if (household == null) {
1007	            return List.of();
1008	        }
1009	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
1010	            .filter(existing -> household.equals(existing.getHouseholdId()))
1011	            .toList();
1012	    }
1013	
1014	    private String householdId(Owner owner) {
1015	        String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
1016	        if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
1017	            return null;
1018	        }
1019	        String key = canonicalizeHousehold(owner.getLastName()) + HOUSEHOLD_KEY_DELIMITER + postcode;
1020	        return sha256Hasher.hexPrefix(key, HOUSEHOLD_ID_LENGTH);
1021	    }
1022	
1023	    /**
1024	     * Number of leading hex characters of the household hash retained as the shared
1025	     * {@code householdId}.
1026	     */
1027	    private static final int HOUSEHOLD_ID_LENGTH = 12;
1028	}
